#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:147
msgid ""
"DSTX is fresh out of the oven — expect a few rough edges. Found a bug? "
"Please report it on GitHub. No warranty, but we'll do our best to fix it."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:148
msgid ""
"DSTX runs as a system service. Close the window? No worries — your LED "
"colors and emulation keep working. After install, log out and back in once — "
"that's it."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:149
msgid ""
"Connect up to 4 controllers at once. Each appears in the left panel with its "
"own independent settings. Customize LED, rumble, deadzone per controller."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:150
msgid ""
"DSTX creates a virtual Xbox 360 pad — works with almost any game. Two modes: "
"<b>UINPUT</b> (full features, rumble included) and <b>UHID</b> "
"(experimental, no rumble but can fix double inputs)."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:151
msgid ""
"The classic, rock‑solid method. Creates virtual devices from user space. "
"Full gamepad capabilities, great compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:152
msgid ""
"Newer kernel module, still experimental. Only handles buttons and axes (no "
"rumble). Can help if you're experiencing double inputs with UINPUT."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:153
msgid ""
"Gyroscope emulation is technically possible but complex — not planned for "
"now. Maybe in a future release!"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:154
msgid ""
"Click the <b>ⓘ</b> button in the top bar to see technical details of your "
"controller: driver, serial, input nodes."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:155
msgid ""
"Prefer the command line? Run <tt>dstx</tt> in your terminal — a full TUI "
"(text interface) is included."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:157
msgid "General Tips"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:161 src/window.vala:158
msgid "Profiles"
msgstr ""

