#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:171
msgid ""
"Create, save, load, or delete profiles. Turn on <b>auto‑save</b> and every "
"change is automatically stored in the current profile."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:172
msgid ""
"Only LED talks directly to your hardware. All other settings apply to the "
"emulated Xbox controller. Keep emulation ON for them to work."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:173
msgid ""
"You choose how the virtual Xbox pad is created. UINPUT is stable and "
"feature‑complete (rumble included). UHID is experimental (no rumble) but can "
"help with double‑input weirdness."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:174
msgid ""
"In UINPUT mode, you can enable/disable rumble and adjust vibration intensity "
"(gain) from 0 to 100%."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:175
msgid ""
"Fine‑tune deadzone (how far you must push before it reacts), sensitivity "
"presets, and invert Y‑axis for left and right sticks independently."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:176
msgid ""
"8 curves available:\n"
"• <b>Default</b> – linear, natural\n"
"• <b>Precision</b> – smooth in the center for tiny moves\n"
"• <b>Rapid</b> – fast response, great for reflexes\n"
"• <b>Smooth</b> – S‑curve: gentle start, faster middle\n"
"• <b>Aggressive</b> – inverted S, quick initial snap\n"
"• <b>Sniper</b> – ultra‑smooth for aiming\n"
"• <b>Racing</b> – linear but longer travel\n"
"• <b>FPS</b> – balanced precision + speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:177
msgid ""
"Flip L2/R2 from analog to digital (on/off). Most games expect analog, but in "
"some niche cases digital can be useful."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:178
msgid ""
"Debounce filters out electrical noise, reducing accidental double presses "
"from the hardware."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:180
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:202 src/window.vala:525
msgid "Controllers"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:215
msgid "Connection hiccups"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:216
msgid "Game not seeing the controller?"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:217
msgid "Steam Input conflict"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:220
msgid ""
"USB and Bluetooth usually work great. If a controller isn't detected, try "
"disconnecting and reconnecting it a couple of times."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:221
msgid ""
"Most games auto‑detect the virtual Xbox pad. If one doesn't, restart the "
"game — that often fixes it."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:222
msgid ""
"DSTX works great with Steam games, but if <b>Steam Input</b> is on, it can "
"interfere. Disable Steam Input when using DSTX, or disable DSTX emulation "
"when using Steam Input."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:224 src/window.vala:833
msgid "Connection"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:228
msgid "USB quirks"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:229
msgid "Bluetooth connections"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:232
msgid ""
"The kernel driver has some bugs over USB — LEDs and rumble may act weird, "
"and double inputs can happen — it's a known issue."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:233
msgid ""
"DualShock 4 behaves much better over Bluetooth. We recommend using Bluetooth "
"for the best experience."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:239
msgid "Solid performer"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:242
msgid ""
"DualSense is the most stable controller so far — USB and Bluetooth both work "
"well. On rare occasions, Bluetooth LED control may fail; just disconnect and "
"reconnect."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:248
msgid "USB works best"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:249
msgid "Bluetooth quirks"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:252
msgid ""
"Best experience is over USB. One catch: unplugging USB automatically "
"reconnects via Bluetooth. If that happens, manually disconnect the "
"controller in your system's Bluetooth settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:253
msgid ""
"Over Bluetooth, analog sticks may show a slight offset (Kernel-related). "
"DSTX applies empirical corrections, but if you still see wrong values, "
"please file a bug report."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:255
msgid "Nintendo Switch Pro"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:290
msgid "Light it up"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:291
msgid "Static Mode"
