#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:294
msgid "Player LEDs (DualSense)"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:297
msgid ""
"Only for DualShock 4 and DualSense. Two modes: Static (fixed color) and "
"Dynamic (moving effects)."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:298
msgid ""
"Pick any color. The LED is written only once, so other apps (Steam, OpenRGB) "
"may overwrite it. Turn on <b>Reapply LED</b> to fight back and keep your "
"color."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:299
msgid ""
"Choose from 8 effects. Depending on the effect, you can set a base color and "
"speed. High speed = more battery drain over Bluetooth."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:300
msgid ""
"Brightness affects both static and dynamic modes. Lower brightness in "
"dynamic mode reduces effect resolution."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:301
msgid ""
"DualSense has small player indicator LEDs (0–4). Set which number lights up."
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:303
msgid "LED Effects"
msgstr ""

#: src/widgets/tips-dialog.vala:307
